String: ### HIP Build Architecture (Pre-compile vs JIT)
- **结论: HIP kernels are pre-compiled at build time, NOT JIT compiled at runtime**
- hipcc/clang++ compiles all `.cu` files into HSACO code objects targeting `CMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES` (gfx1151)
- These are embedded into the shared libraries (`libggml-hip.so`, `libdflash27b.a`)
- At runtime: only loading of pre-compiled code objects, no compilation
- Key difference: CUDA can compile kernels at runtime via NVRTC/NVVM; HIP has no equivalent JIT by default
- The "kernel compilation" at runtime in CUDA is via NVRTC/NVVM; HIP does not use NVVM-like JIT compilation
- The hang during initialization is therefore NOT caused by runtime kernel compilation

## Learnings:
- **Pattern discovered:** HIP on ROCm pre-compiles kernels via hipcc at build time for specified `CMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES`
- **Key files:** `dflash/deps/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-hip/CMakeLists.txt` contains the build configuration
- **Gotcha:** CUDA can JIT-compile via NVRTC; HIP cannot — all kernels must be pre-compiled
- **Conclusion:** The initialization hang is NOT caused by JIT kernel compilation on HIP/gfx1151</tool_use_error>][0m
